  "text": "And why isn't the public getting respected here with all this money coming in on Tampa? Another prime time? Maybe because the public doesn't actually move lines for major markets like sides, totals, and money lines. Maybe because all the books that feed into something like Pickett are in effect rec books, aka those books that kick out winning bettors, aka those books where they feel very confident that their clientele do not have an edge against them in the aggregate. Why would they move the line based on public information coming in? They wouldn't. They don't. Good night.",
